# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored and must stay that way.
#
# WHAT IS AND IS NOT WIRED UP, as of 2026-09-08:
#   - Market-data clients ARE wired up and read these variables: live/alpaca.py,
#     live/polygon.py, data/fred.py, scripts/fetch_macro.py. They are written
#     from published API references and were UNVERIFIED on any wire until first
#     contact; see docs/SETUP.md "What is unverified" and ticket T-524425f9.
#   - Order routing is NOT wired up and raises: brokers/base.py, and the
#     connector skeletons in data/connectors.py. The Binance and Deribit keys
#     below exist so the shape is settled, not so orders can be placed.
#
# Rules, enforced in code rather than left to discipline:
#   - Values are read from the environment only. No file loading, no defaults.
#     See src/trading_platform/core/credentials.py; tests/test_connectors.py
#     asserts the string "dotenv" never appears in it.
#   - A credential never prints itself; repr and str are redacted, so a secret
#     cannot reach a log or traceback by accident.
#   - Blank is treated as absent, so a half-configured environment fails the
#     same way an unconfigured one does.
#
# Scope discipline:
#   - READ-ONLY market data scopes only. Nothing here needs trading permission.
#   - NEVER enable withdrawal permission on a key used with this project.
#   - Never paste a key into a source file, a prompt, or a commit message. A
#     PreToolUse hook blocks credential-shaped writes, but do not rely on it.
#
# For a real machine, prefer ~/.config/trading_platform/env at chmod 600 over a
# .env inside the repository: .gitignore does not cover a mistake made outside
# it. docs/SETUP.md section 4 has the heredoc. deploy/install.sh creates that
# file empty and never writes a value into it.


# --- The store ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Required by the collector, the reconciler, the operations page, the health
# check and the paper runner (store/connection.py). Without it the paper runner
# still journals, but nothing is queryable and NOTHING GATES LEVERAGE, so a
# session holding a leveraged instrument is refused rather than run blind.
# The docker-compose development database listens on 5439, deliberately off
# 5432 so it cannot collide with a Postgres you already depend on.
TRADING_PLATFORM_DSN=

# The database the store-backed tests run against. Set it and 111 tests stop
# skipping (1,307 collected, 1,196 of them database-free).
TRADING_PLATFORM_TEST_DSN=

# Set to 1 to make the store tests REQUIRED rather than optional: a missing
# driver, a missing DSN or an unreachable database becomes a failure instead of
# a skip. CI and `scripts/dev_postgres.sh env` both set it. This is what stops a
# run that quietly lost its database from reporting green over 20-odd skips.
# See tests/test_store_guard.py (corpus entry G02).
TRADING_PLATFORM_STORE_TESTS_REQUIRED=


# --- Alpaca market data ------------------------------------------------------
# live/alpaca.py, data/alpaca.py, scripts/run_paper.py. Read-only data key.
# A paper-trading key from the Alpaca dashboard is fine; a live-trading key is
# not needed and must not be used — nothing here routes orders.
#
# The free tier serves the IEX tape ALONE, not the consolidated market. In
# collector.toml that means venue = "iex", not "sip". Calling IEX "sip" makes
# every Alpaca-versus-Polygon difference read as basis and turns every genuine
# bad print into a shrug; the collector refuses the config that says it.
APCA_API_KEY_ID=
APCA_API_SECRET_KEY=


# --- Polygon market data -----------------------------------------------------
# live/polygon.py, data/polygon.py. Polygon aggregates are consolidated, so a
# source using this key is venue = "sip".
POLYGON_API_KEY=


# --- FRED / ALFRED macro data ------------------------------------------------
# scripts/fetch_macro.py, data/fred.py. ALFRED rather than FRED on purpose: a
# macro series is stored BY VINTAGE, because the value a release had on the day
# is not the value it has after revision, and a backtest that reads today's
# revision of a 2019 print has read the future.
FRED_API_KEY=


# --- Binance -----------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT REQUIRED. Klines and funding history are public endpoints, and
# scripts/fetch_binance.py reaches them with no key at all. BinanceConnector
# deliberately declares no credentials.
#
# These two are listed only because BinanceBroker (live order routing) would
# need them. That broker is intentionally unimplemented — see docs/PLAN.md
# Phase 6. Leave these blank unless you are doing something the roadmap does
# not currently contain.
BINANCE_API_KEY=
BINANCE_API_SECRET=


# --- Deribit (crypto options, roadmap steps 41-46) ---------------------------
# Public candles need no auth, but the options chain and instrument metadata
# page more easily with a read-only client credential pair. No code reads these
# yet: data/connectors.py raises.
DERIBIT_CLIENT_ID=
DERIBIT_CLIENT_SECRET=


# --- Tickets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Overrides the path to the ticket event log (tickets/store.py). Leave blank to
# use harness/tickets/events.jsonl, which is what you want outside tests.
TRADING_PLATFORM_TICKETS=
